%% How the cluster's Python environment is built, and how every job checks it.
%% Shown in docs/project/running.md.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor You
  participant Setup as setup_remote.sh<br/>(your machine)
  participant Login as Login node
  participant Serial as all_serial<br/>(Slurm step)
  participant Job as A job<br/>(later)

  You->>Setup: setup_remote.sh, after uv.lock changes
  Setup->>Login: create folders, set the cluster's uv to your version
  Setup->>Login: copy the code
  Setup->>Serial: srun: build the environment
  Serial->>Serial: delete the lock hash: from now on, jobs refuse to start
  Serial->>Serial: uv sync --locked, with a temporary cache in the node's /tmp
  Serial->>Serial: write the hash of uv.lock, delete the cache
  Serial-->>Setup: done
  Note over Login,Serial: a failed build leaves no hash: jobs keep refusing until a build succeeds

  Job->>Job: compare the run's uv.lock hash with the environment's
  alt they match
    Job->>Job: run the command
  else they differ, or no hash
    Job->>Job: stop: "run setup_remote.sh" (status: failed)
  end
